      <p class="il-prediction" data-cause-note></p>
      <div class="il-group" data-group data-unlocks="retrieve">
        <p class="il-question">What is your ruling?</p>
        {customerRuling.map((o) => <button type="button" data-why={o.why} data-correct={o.correct ? "" : undefined}>{o.label}</button>)}
        <p class="il-feedback" role="status"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="il-group" data-group data-unlock="retrieve" data-retrieve>
      <p class="il-question">Your next AI-built join looks clean. Choose the three things you would ask for.</p>
      {asks.map((a) => <button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-ask data-good={a.correct ? "" : undefined} data-miss={a.miss}>{a.label}</button>)}
      <button type="button" class="il-next" data-check-asks>Check my three</button>
      <p class="il-feedback" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="il-after il-close">
      <h3 tabindex="-1">Before you trust any AI-built join, ask for three things</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Entity counts before and after.</strong> Then have every change explained. {data.schools.clean} schools became {data.schools.merged} here, and nobody asked why.</li>
        <li><strong>Records that cannot be true.</strong> A team playing itself. An order placed before the account existed.</li>
        <li><strong>Every merge it made.</strong> A false merge raises no error, so if you cannot review the merges, you cannot defend the number.</li>
